lunza, etc.)","evidence":"No reports of armed-group activity in rural Makanza territory as of 2026; state presence through police posts and secteur administration, with customary chiefs handling local disputes. River banditry/piracy is occasional and not territorial.","unit":"CD4105-makanza","run_id":"drc-swarm-1","source_ids":[30]},{"controller_id":"cod-pnc","sovereign_id":"cod","status":"dominant","confidence":"low","basis":"default_state_presence","as_of":"2026-10-01","zone":"Southern villages in Mampoko health zone (Nganda Mpaka, Limbila)","evidence":"Remote riverine villages with no reported armed-group activity; assessed as default state presence.","unit":"CD4105-makanza","run_id":"drc-swarm-1","source_ids":[30]},{"controller_id":"cod-pnc","sovereign_id":"cod","status":"dominant","confidence":"medium","basis":"default_state_presence","as_of":"2026-10-01","zone":"Makanza (Mankanza) town, territory seat, all quarters","evidence":"Territory seat with state administration on the Congo River; no reports of armed-group presence in 2025-2026 searches. Policing assumed by PNC with FARDC/naval elements present; past banditry has not translated into non-state control.","unit":"CD4105-makanza","run_id":"drc-swarm-1","presence":[{"entity_id":"cod-fardc","role":"present"}],"source_ids":[30]}],"sources":{"30":{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Makanza_Territory","title":"Makanza Territory","publisher":"Wikipedia"}},"units":{"CD4105-makanza":"Makanza (Mankanza) territory in Equateur lies along the main Congo River channel, far from the eastern conflict zones; no armed group is reported to hold any territory there. The territory seat Makanza town is administered by the state, with the Congolese National Police handling day-to-day order and FARDC/naval elements present on the river. Historical banditry and river piracy have been reported but there is no evidence of a non-state actor exercising control. Rural villages (Makanza and Mampoko health zones) are assessed as default state (PNC) presence with low-medium confidence given scarce reporting."}}